paperboy (0.14.1a-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * "Recommended for you" appears after the first read or thumbs up and always fills with the best-matching articles
  * Fixed a freeze when a feed's articles contain malformed numeric character entities
  * Faster article card rendering: viewed and saved checks no longer read the disk or scan every saved article
  * Feed and image processing compile their regular expressions once instead of on every call
  * Log failures to save viewed state or back up a damaged config file instead of ignoring them
  * The onboarding country page icon now matches the dimmed color of the large icons on the other pages
  * Preferences opens faster: its source, feed, podcast, magazine and category subpages are built on first open, the article cache size is measured off the main thread, and followed-feed logos load on a background thread pool
  * Fixed reference-cycle leaks that kept every podcast, podcast hero, magazine and score card alive, and every article, podcast and sidebar context-menu popover, after they were removed
  * Free closed pop-up article sheets and per-card save-animation state, and cap the Google News URL and reading-time prefetch caches at 2000 entries
  * Fixed the restored podcast session losing its cover art: keep the saved cover copy instead of overwriting its path with NULL when it isn't in MetaCache, download the cover directly when it isn't cached, name each copy per episode, and update the player bar and MPRIS when a late cover arrives
  * Added a My Library podcasts page with an Up Next row of in-progress and newest unplayed episodes, and a grid of subscribed shows sorted by latest episode
  * Up Next cards show the release time, a "New" tag, and a play button with the time left, with a progress bar once an episode has been started
  * Library show cards show the publisher, last update time, and a count of new episodes
  * Searching on My Library filters subscribed shows by name, publisher, or category
  * Podcast categories are read from PodcastIndex and stored with each subscription, and existing subscriptions get theirs from their feed
  * The sidebar's Podcasts section has My Library with a total new-episode badge, and subscribed shows in a collapsible "Shows" list with cover art
  * Sidebar icons are centered in a single column, fixing glyph icons and the "+" on Add RSS Feed and Add a Podcast sitting off-center
  * Fixed sidebar podcast covers sometimes missing at startup: switching pages no longer drops image downloads that aren't tied to a page, such as sidebar and player covers

 -- Isaac Joseph <calamityjoe87@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

paperboy (0.14.0a-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Added a Country setting (Preferences > Personalization > Region) with the 87 Google News country and language editions, set to Automatic by default from the system's time zone and language
  * Added a "Where Are You Reading From?" onboarding page to check or change the detected country
  * Outside the US, "US News" becomes the country's national news, with a flag icon for light and dark mode
  * Outside the US, the Front Page, Trending, and each category's Google News section show the country's news in its language
  * NPR, WSJ, the New York Times, and Bloomberg searches always use Google News' US edition so they return a full set of articles
  * Local News now asks for a postal code and prefers results in the user's country
  * Place names with mixed casing are kept as written, and two-letter town names are no longer capitalized as US states
  * Added translation support, with translations for Portuguese (Brazil), Spanish, French, German, Italian, Russian, Japanese, and Simplified Chinese
  * Added Portuguese (Portugal), Dutch, Polish, Turkish, Korean, Ukrainian, Traditional Chinese (Taiwan, Hong Kong), Indonesian, Vietnamese, Arabic, and Hebrew translations
  * Scroll arrows keep their sides and scrolling titles in right-to-left scripts scroll correctly
  * Translated the desktop file's name, description, and keywords
  * The AppImage now bundles the translations
  * Country names, national and Local News headers, and category names in page headers are now translated
  * Fixed some interface text never being offered for translation
  * Article times and dates now use the interface language's wording and date order
  * Translated the remaining English notifications, buttons, and dialogs, the reading time, the built-in outlets' descriptions, and email share text
  * Counts and search results now use the right plural in every language, including languages with several plural forms
  * Cache sizes use the locale's units and decimal separator
  * Market prices use the locale's number format; chart hover times follow the clock setting
  * Translated the remaining English text, including weather highs and lows, follow tooltips, podcast and magazine messages, and fallback names
  * Article bylines now follow the system's 12-hour or 24-hour clock setting
  * Fixed failed feeds showing a spinner until timeout instead of an error in languages other than English
  * Fixed dates on older article cards sometimes being a day off, and the header date padding the day with a zero
  * Added a Contributors page to the About dialog
  * Websites are asked for pages in the user's language
  * Fixed reader view failing on pages that aren't in UTF-8
  * Fixed the Front Page's hero carousel sometimes not appearing after picking a new country
  * Added sports score cards for tennis (ATP, WTA), golf (PGA Tour, LPGA Tour, DP World Tour), racing (Formula 1, NASCAR Cup Series, IndyCar), and PFL, off by default
  * Golf and racing cards show the top three places with flags, with tied golfers sharing a place; tennis cards show games per set
  * Tennis, golf, and racing cards show the tournament or race and the round or session
  * Tennis shows recent and upcoming main-draw singles matches only; Formula 1 skips practice sessions
  * Golf tournaments that haven't started show their date instead of "TBD", on the right day in every time zone
  * Added 16 regional football and rugby leagues, on by default and listed first in the countries that follow them
  * Added Leagues and Section Order pages to Preferences' Sports Score Cards, with leagues grouped by region
  * US pro leagues are on by default only in the US and Canada, college leagues only in the US
  * Onboarding's sports page now groups leagues by region like Preferences, with section order set in Preferences
  * Fixed Trending sometimes showing 9 stories instead of 10 on load, with the last one appearing about 20 seconds later

